                <pb facs="0133" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Provisional/88: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-25T09:00:00+09:00">March 25, 1938—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>205. Nanking’s 82, March 23, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d137-f1"/> Nanking
                    Provisional Government. In reference to reports of impending inauguration at
                    Nanking of a provisional government, Foreign Minister Hirota has stated in the
                    House of Representatives that Japan’s relations with the existing Peiping regime
                    will not thereby be changed; that Japan expects that the Peiping regime will in
                    time develop into a unified administration for both North and Central China; but
                    that in the meantime commercial interests contemplating activities in Central
                    China must deal with the impending Nanking regime.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai for Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
